+# MarufYT .8 — IPA URL and network endpoint audit
+
+Date: 2026-11-03, Asia/Kuala_Lumpur. Audit only; no application changes, rebuild,
+release replacement, branch change, commit or push. Repository revision:
+`81c31676d91c94e47c905ebe31b1cf6fcb1b62ba`, branch `final-update-security`.
+The existing release report identifies compiled source as
+`c5f3dc3f8aa2205053b27029f2e73552d80fae28`.
+
+## 1. Executive conclusion
+
+**Findings identified: one Low conditional URL-validation gap and three
+Informational observations**, with evidence below. No Critical or High issue was
+demonstrated by this audit. This is not a runtime safety certification.
+
+Every outer IPA file was scanned. The retained inventory contains **818 HTTP(S)/WS
+literal records**, not 818 active connections: **795 common, 8 Latest-only and 15
+Stable-only**. Some records are templates, metadata, examples, regular expressions,
+or decoder artifacts. There are 221 HTTP, 596 HTTPS and one WS record; no WSS
+literal was recovered. **39 URL records occur in MarufYT components, all common**
+to both packages. This includes dependency documentation strings and shared Google
+destinations, not just MarufYT-added requests. The injected MarufYT dylib is
+byte-identical between builds.
+
+No iPhone capture or signed-app execution was available. Five credential-free
+public-fixture GET probes ran from Windows; these do not establish app traffic.
+No malicious destination or unexpected credential-upload path was established
+within the examined MarufYT source paths. Original YouTube's complete compiled
+network call graph and all dynamically supplied destinations remain unresolved.
+
