+Example reading an annex without extracting it: Python
+`csv.DictReader(gzip.open(path, 'rt', encoding='utf-8-sig'))`.
+The files can also be decompressed with a standard gzip-compatible archive tool.
+
+Methods: scan all uncompressed member bytes, printable ASCII/UTF-8-compatible
+strings, raw UTF-8 URIs, ASCII-range UTF-16 LE/BE views, complete Mach-O `__ustring`
+sections; decode supported plist/JSON/text, percent/HTML/escaped-slash forms,
+recognizable URL/base64 patterns and PEM certificate DER strings. One bounded
+nested ZIP/gzip layer is inspected. All injected dylibs, host/framework Mach-O files,
+plists, readable scripts/configurations and resources are included in outer coverage.
+Scanner and classifier are retained beside the evidence for review/reproduction.
+
+Offsets generally identify the enclosing string/container, not necessarily the
+exact token byte; heuristic occurrence counts may duplicate alternate decoding
+views. Raw certificate DER can append printable bytes such as `0` to a URL.
+Opposite-alignment UTF-16, format specifiers and percent decoding of `%%` templates
+also produce artifacts. Preserve evidence, but do not resolve/probe these as real
+hosts. Source functions for opaque original-host strings remain explicitly UNKNOWN;
+no fictional function-level attribution or runtime data flow is asserted.
+
+Domain classification is by recognizable service family and containing component,
+not an independently verified registrant lookup. Google/YouTube families include
+`youtube.com`, `youtubei.googleapis.com`, `googlevideo.com`, `ytimg.com`,
+`googleusercontent.com`, `accounts.google.com` and related Google services.
+Advertising/telemetry-shaped host strings include `googleadservices.com`,
+`doubleclick.net`, `app-analytics-services.com`, `app-ads-services.com` and
+`firebaseinstallations.googleapis.com`. Other records include Apple/PKI certificate
+locations, XML/XMP namespaces, dependency documentation and unknown candidates.
+Their occurrence alone proves neither tracking nor malicious behavior.
