+## 5. Transport, redirects, addresses and schemes
+
+MarufYT's inspected fixed remote request URLs use HTTPS. `URLPolicy.h:9–13` requires
+HTTPS, nonempty host, no URL username/password and nil/443 port. Its guarded client
+rejects invalid initial URLs; local file imports are separate filesystem paths.
+`URLPolicy.mm:10–28` validates previous and next redirect URLs, rejects generic
+cross-origin body/stream replay and removes headers except a small public allowlist.
+Media redirects also require trusted `googlevideo.com` exact/suffix hosts and a
+media header allowlist. Same-origin legitimate auth is preserved. SABR's custom
+protobuf redirect is checked separately. A redirect policy does not validate
+arbitrary sensitive query parameters that a caller deliberately includes in a URL.
+
+No custom trust-all/invalid-certificate acceptance handler was identified in the
+inspected MarufYT request layer; Foundation system trust applies there. This is
+not proof of pinning, original-host TLS internals, dependency-wide trust behavior
+or all AVFoundation child requests. HLS handoff is outside this guarded client.
+
+221 HTTP records include schema/DTD/XMP identifiers, PKI OCSP/CRL metadata,
+examples and original-host strings. They are not 221 demonstrated cleartext calls.
+Both host Info.plists permit local networking and insecure HTTP for these inherited
+carrier domains: `cpid.ddt.telenor.io`, `nwp.t-mobile.com`,
+`vaspbon-int.msg.t-mobile.com`, `vaspbonstg-int.msg.t-mobile.com`.
+No global arbitrary-load permission was identified in these ATS dictionaries.
+
+The sole WS record, `N000965`, is an original executable format template, rendered
+as `ws://[userinfo-redacted]@:%d/%@`; it is not a usable observed destination.
+No WSS literal was extracted; runtime WebSocket construction is still possible.
+Inbound schemes and allowed query schemes may open/receive callbacks from another
+app rather than contact a network server. All are listed in the scheme annex.
+
+IPv4 candidates include loopback `127.0.0.1`, private/link-local ranges, masks,
+`224.0.0.251` and `239.255.255.250` discovery addresses, `8.8.8.8`, and version-like
+tuples. Their exact files are in the IP annex. No hardcoded-IP MarufYT exfiltration
+request was established. IPv6-shaped text also includes syntax coincidences.
+None of these addresses was probed. Integer sockaddr values, DNS answers and
+runtime LAN peer addresses are outside literal extraction.
+
