+## 7. Findings and privacy implications
+
+### U-01 — HLS manifest handoff lacks local secure-URL validation — Low
+
+Both builds. `Tweak/Features/Streaming/HLSPlayback.mm`,
+`YTKACEHLSFetchVisionThen:173–177` caches `streamingData.hlsManifestUrl` when nonempty;
+`YTKACEHLSSwap:232–237` selects cached/native text and calls `setHlsManifestURL:`
+without `MarufYTIsSecureURL` at that boundary. `YTKACEHLSEnabled:45` requires playback
+fix mode 2; it is not the default. The binary contains the manifest key/setter and
+HLS diagnostic literals; exact offsets are recorded in final verification.
+
+This is a confirmed local hardening gap, **not a demonstrated remote exploit or
+observed HTTP request**. An unsafe upstream/modified/native URL is a prerequisite;
+the normal player response arrives over HTTPS. The original host may independently
+validate/block it or ATS may prevent cleartext. If accepted, the chosen host could
+learn IP/request metadata; whether tokens/cookies are attached is unknown. No
+contacts/photos/files exposure was demonstrated. Recommended future fix: validate
+the selected URL before cache insertion and native handoff, with safe fallback;
+also test manifest child URLs/redirects on device. No code was changed.
+
+### U-02 — Inherited carrier HTTP exceptions — Informational
+
+Both `Payload/YouTube.app/Info.plist`, `NSAppTransportSecurity`; four domains listed
+in section 5. These allow specific insecure host loads, not proof such requests
+occur. If used, data on HTTP could be observable/modifiable in transit; exact
+payload/auth is unknown. Recommendation: capture the native carrier flows before
+considering narrower exceptions; do not remove host compatibility policy blindly.
+
+### U-03 — Optional integrations and host attribution can disclose activity — Informational
+
+Evidence: SponsorClient, SponsorMenu, DeArrow, AiSList and host conversion templates
+in sections 4/6 and occurrence annex. Normal lookup/DeArrow can disclose full video
+IDs; reporting/submissions disclose selected content and contributor/reporter data;
+private prefix lookup is not universal privacy protection. Host attribution strings
+suggest possible IDFA-related fields, without proving collection or transmission.
+No unauthorized sensitive upload was confirmed. Recommendation: explain integration
+data flows, retain opt-in controls and verify actual ATT/telemetry behavior by capture.
+
+### U-04 — Opaque host and dynamic destinations remain unverified — Informational
+
+Evidence: unknown function/reachability/auth fields in the inventory, runtime
+signed media URLs, HLS, generic object-provided image/caption URLs and host binaries.
+Not every string has a recoverable original-source function. Native DNS/config,
+protobuf, redirects, JS-built URLs, encryption/obfuscation and runtime account
+state prevent a closed static destination list. Recommendation: controlled signed
+device capture with disposable test account, service toggles and redirect scenarios.
+This limitation is not itself proof of a vulnerability or hidden connection.
+
+## 8. Tests and actual network observations
+
+Both package SHA-256/ZIP CRC checks passed; all members received lexical scanning.
+Binary parse/section evidence and unchanged repository branch/HEAD/tracked diff are
+recorded in final verification. **Four existing security source-contract tests
+passed** ([log](URL_NETWORK_EVIDENCE/SOURCE_CONTRACT_TESTS.txt)); these inspect source
+contracts and do not execute Foundation/iPhone networking or prove full coverage.
+No application binary was executed and no app rebuild was performed.
+
+Controlled public-fixture probes used Python urllib on Windows with default
+certificate/hostname validation, no proxies, cookies, Authorization, API key or
+account credentials. Redirects were restricted to same-host HTTPS/443; none occurred.
+The fixture video ID `dQw4w9WgXcQ` is public test content, not personal watch history.
+
+| GET fixture | Observed result |
+| --- | --- |
+| SponsorBlock normal lookup, public ID, sponsor category | HTTP 404; response alone does not show a client defect or security issue |
+| SponsorBlock private lookup, SHA-256 prefix `5f6b` | HTTP 200, JSON list of 43 entries |
+| YouTube oEmbed for same public ID | HTTP 200 |
+| AiSList GitHub blocklist | HTTP 200 |
+| AiSList GitHub warnlist | HTTP 200 |
+
+Exact request URLs, response metadata and bounded body hashes/shapes are in
+[controlled observations](URL_NETWORK_EVIDENCE/CONTROLLED_NETWORK_OBSERVATIONS.json).
+Bodies were not retained. Services could see the audit PC's public IP/timing.
+No DeArrow request, POST/report/vote, suspicious candidate probe or credential test
+was sent. These are **five PC observations**, not app/iPhone traffic, TLS pinning
+validation or runtime redirect-policy tests.
+
+## 9. Remaining device tests and exact limitations
+
+NOT TESTED: signed launch and Google login/account switching; per-feature traffic
+with toggles off/on; cookies/Authorization on real redirects; mode-2 HLS parent,
+child manifests and segments; background requests; Cast/LAN/IPv6; actual telemetry,
+ATT/IDFA, WS/WSS and server-selected routes. Use a disposable authorized test
+account and redact captures; never upload real credentials into audit artifacts.
+
+The inventory is complete for the scanner's retained lexical output over every
+outer member, **not a claim that every possible runtime endpoint was recovered**.
+Proprietary compressed formats, encrypted strings, arbitrary encodings, executable
+control flow and dynamically returned URLs are not exhaustively decoded. Raw
+string matches do not establish DNS ownership, active connections, permission use,
+request bodies or exploitability. No 100% security claim is made.
+
+**Conclusion: findings identified — one Low conditional HLS validation gap and
+three Informational observations. Both IPAs and application source remain unchanged;
+actual iPhone network behavior remains untested.**
